<title>USA: CIT Group sets $100 mln in notes.</title>
<headline>CIT Group sets $100 mln in notes.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following debt issue from CIT Group Holdings was priced on Tuesday, according to sole manager Lehman Brothers.</p>
<p>BORROWER CIT GROUP HOLDINGS</p>
<p>AMT $100 MLN	 COUPON 5.875 PCT  MATURITY 11/09/1998</p>
<p>TYPE NOTES	   ISS PRICE 99.953  FIRST PAY DATE 11/09/1997</p>
<p>LAST MOODY'S AA3   YIELD 5.90 PCT    PAY FREQ SEMI-ANNUAL</p>
<p>LAST S&amp;P A-PLUS    SPREAD +17 BP     CALLABLE NO</p>
<p>NOTE: CIT GROUP HOLDINGS IS 80 PERCENT OWNED BY DAI-ICHI</p>
<p>KANGYO BANK LTD AND 20 PERCENT BY CHASE MANHATTAN CORP</p>
<p>U.S. corporate bond unit, 212 859-1678</p>
</text>
